NAME
    qemu-combined-test.sh - run BIOS, UEFI x86_64 and UEFI ARM64 on one image

SYNOPSIS
    tests/qemu-combined-test.sh --output DIR [--stages DIR]
                                [--bios-modules-dir DIR]
                                [--modules-bios DIR] [--modules-x64 DIR]
                                [--modules-arm64 DIR] [--prepare-only]
                                [--target all|i386-pc|x86_64-efi|arm64-efi]

DESCRIPTION
    Without --stages, calls build.sh three times for the BIOS, UEFI x64
    and UEFI ARM64 targets, using the three tracked module archives
    automatically when present and verified. Target-specific modules may be supplied
    explicitly using the --modules-* options. With --stages, uses
    prebuilt target directories from other compatible Linux build hosts.
    Calls qemu-combined-image.sh to create one new raw GPT disk.
    By default sequentially runs qemu-run.sh on that SAME disk, first
    as BIOS x86_64, then UEFI x86_64, then UEFI ARM64; each QEMU
    instance must be closed to proceed. --target selects one target
    from the three, while still preparing the common disk.

    --prepare-only creates the image without running QEMU; one can then
    inspect the unchanged file manually under each firmware, without
    root for the qemu-run.sh portion.

EXAMPLES
    sudo tests/qemu-combined-test.sh --output ./combined-qemu --prepare-only

    tests/qemu-run.sh --target i386-pc \
      --image ./combined-qemu/m-boot-combined.raw
    tests/qemu-run.sh --target x86_64-efi \
      --image ./combined-qemu/m-boot-combined.raw
    tests/qemu-run.sh --target arm64-efi \
      --image ./combined-qemu/m-boot-combined.raw

    sudo tests/qemu-combined-test.sh --stages ./prebuilt-stages \
      --output ./combined-qemu --target all

THREE TARGET MODULE SETS AND STAGES STORED IN GIT
    The repository tracks complete x86_64-efi, arm64-efi and i386-pc module/stage
    archives. No time-limited GitHub artifact download is required.
    After git pull, verify the three package SHA256 files and extract them
    to a common STAGES directory:
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-x86_64-efi.tar.xz.sha256
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz.sha256
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz.sha256
        mkdir -p ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-x86_64-efi.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages
    All three stages are already built, so --stages remains available.
    The regular invocation with only --output builds fresh stages from
    the current source and verified archives. --bios-modules-dir is
    optional because boot.img is also resolved from the verified BIOS
    archive. The BIOS path still
    requires the host command grub-bios-setup (grub2-common); no target
    module packages need to be installed on the host. See manual/build and prebuilt/README.md.


REQUIREMENTS
    Linux root to prepare virtual GPT/mount filesystems, three target
    GRUB module sets or prebuilt stages, i386-pc boot.img, GRUB BIOS
    setup, plus QEMU emulators and OVMF/AAVMF firmware for interactive
    execution. Cross-host stages must be from compatible GRUB versions
    and contain the same loader/ tree. If a native ARM64 GRUB module
    package is unavailable on an x86_64 host, produce that stage on
    an ARM64 build host and pass --stages after collecting all stages.

RESULTS
    BIOS boot and both UEFI boots must reach the external m-loader TEST
    menu on the SAME raw image. A started QEMU process is not enough
    evidence of boot success. Neither physical USB nor secure boot is
    tested by this workflow.

